    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d546-a1">

                <pb facs="0743" n="649" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg649"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 600.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Duke of Tetuan to Mr. Taylor.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ministry of
                            State</hi>, <lb/>
                        <placeName type="venue"><hi rendition="#italic">Palace</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1896-11-03"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November 3, 1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: In addition to my note of the 21st
                    ultimo, relative to the proceedings instituted in Cuba against the naturalized
                    American citizen, Manuel Fernandez Chaqueilo, I have the honor to inform your
                    excellency that, as reported in a telegram from the Captain-General of the said
                    island to the minister of war, Fernandez Chaqueilo was caught with arms in hand
                    and consequently he will be tried by the war <pb facs="0744" n="650"
                        xml:id="pg650"/> jurisdiction in ordinary trial, in strict accordance with
                    the protocol of January 12, 1877. This decision has been duly communicated to
                    the consul-general of the United States at Habana.</p>
                <p>I avail myself, etc.,</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">The Duke of Tetuan.</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
